        "comments": "Modern sugarcane cultivar varieties are a result of interspecific hybridization between two highly polyploid species, 'Saccharum officinarum' (2n=80) and 'Saccharum spontaneum' (2n=40-128). Successive backcrosses between the original hybrid and progenitor species, in order to recover specific traits, resulted in a highly heterozygous, aneuploid genome, with 10-13 sets of 10 basic chromosomes. The Saccharum hybrid cultivarSP80-3280 genome is composed mostly from 'S. officinarum', but 10-15% from 'S. spontaneum' and\n5% with recombined chromosomes between those two progenitors.",
